  "visual_review": "Direct review of both held1024px prompts at initial/500/1000, CFG4 seed63: both calibrations improve large color areas and coarse figure/face/hand/food structure from their own initial images by500. Independent p28 improves further at1000; native-moment p28 retains a coherent scene but has more fragmented surface texture than at500. Both p31 images develop stronger clipping/fine fragmentation from500 to1000. Improvement is prompt-dependent and not monotonic. No clear native-moment visual advantage is demonstrated; retain the production calibration policy. Remaining artifacts do not prove long-training inability, and lower loss is not broad visual-quality acceptance."
